
After completing ALL work below, stop and hand control back to the parent loop. Do not run Shark status-transition commands yourself; report the recommended outcome in your final response so the parent can advance the workflow.

Prepare a repair plan for E07-F01 from docs/plan/E07/E07-F01/E07-F01.md, its research report, related decisions, prior findings, and affected production callers. Register the plan as a related document; identify it by path and content hash. State the diagnosis, approach, preserved behavior, constraints, scope, assertions and review baseline. Maintain one coverage index: obligation, authoritative source, production caller or boundary, planned change, required assertions, and current evidence. Reference existing decisions; escalate conflicting authority to its owner. Keep all findings and route to the earliest invalidated stage. Diagnosis changes invalidate the plan and downstream evidence; material plan changes invalidate approval; candidate changes invalidate review and QA. Reuse unchanged valid evidence. Unavailable external evidence is blocked, not acceptance.
Simple bugs may use brief evidence; recurrent, uncertain, stateful, accounting and cross-boundary bugs require deeper analysis. Return needs_research for a causal gap, blocked for unavailable external evidence, and pass only for a reviewable plan. The parent owns transitions.

End with `RECOMMENDED OUTCOME: pass`, `RECOMMENDED OUTCOME: needs_research`, `RECOMMENDED OUTCOME: fail`, or `RECOMMENDED OUTCOME: blocked` as appropriate. Use fail for an unresolved plan.
